WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.674
Meet WorkStep, an AI development workspace for individual developers and small teams.

2
00:00:05.624 --> 00:00:09.733
Let AI work step by step, while you review the results that matter.

3
00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:14.490
Connect AI coding tools like Codex and Claude Code.

4
00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:20.158
Install and verify one execution engine to get started, then choose the right engine for each step.

5
00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:23.733
Describe how you want to work.

6
00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:29.400
Review the workflow assistant’s proposal, then adjust steps, connections, and settings on the canvas.

7
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.629
Analyze, implement, test, and review.

8
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:40.818
Define inputs and outputs so the implementation step receives the analysis plan, and testing and review receive the changes.

9
00:00:40.768 --> 00:00:45.247
Run tasks by dependency, and reuse the workflow for your next task.

10
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.420
Follow execution progress, tool calls, and output files.

11
00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.206
Add human review to important steps.

12
00:00:53.206 --> 00:00:57.719
Approve to continue, or send feedback and return the step for another pass.

13
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.448
Share a project with authorized WorkStep devices to follow tasks and review results together.

14
00:01:04.398 --> 00:01:06.712
Project data stays local.

15
00:01:06.712 --> 00:01:12.025
When you use an external model, task context is still sent according to your engine settings.

16
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:17.093
Download WorkStep and verify your first execution engine.

17
00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:20.503
Start with a small task whose result you can inspect.

18
00:01:20.503 --> 00:01:25.052
Give every step a clear outcome, and keep the important decisions in your hands.
